# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Voidloom — CODE IN, DATA AND MODELS OUT.
# Written BEFORE `git init`: git must never see the brain's contents, only its
# machinery. A nightly DB snapshot preserves the MEMORIES; this repo preserves
# the MACHINERY. They are different jobs and they stay separate. (#13479)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── THE BRAIN ITSELF — never, under any circumstance ──
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
seed-dbs/

# ── DERIVED / BULK — local history and workspaces ──
archives/
ACE_Workspaces/

# ── RUNTIME STATE + CACHES (regenerated; some are 0600 by design) ──
THINKER_RECORD
THINKER_LOG
.THINKER_RECORD.tmp.*
pre_cognitive_cache.json
.voidloom_notify_state.json
.affect_scan_state.json
cognitive_map.html
eval/ab_comparison_results.json

# ── THE OLD VERSION CONTROL SYSTEM ──
# Hand-named .bak copies from before version control. Git is the history now;
# these stay on disk and out of the repo.
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.orig
*.pre-*
# ...and the UNDERSCORE spelling. `*.pre-*` (hyphen) correctly ignored 30+ files
# and silently admitted `session_start_inject.py.pre_voidloom`, which then reached
# the delivered package. A pattern written from the examples in front of you
# matches the examples; write it from the DEFINITION of the set instead.
*.pre_*

# ── PYTHON / TOOLING NOISE ──
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ── SECRETS — belt and braces; nothing here today and it stays that way ──
*.env
.env*
*.key
*.pem
*credentials*
*token*.json
rclone.conf

# ── EDITOR / OS ──
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# ── PACKAGE ARTIFACTS — admitted BY EXPLICIT NAME, never by relaxing *.db ──
# claude_memory_blank.db is SCHEMA-ONLY (36 tables, 0 memories, 573 KB): it is
# machinery, not a brain. seed_pack.json is the memories a fresh install loads
# and embeds with the model its hardware sweep chose — ONE text file we can
# diff and review, never two pre-built binary DBs that drift from it. (#6387)
!seed/claude_memory_blank.db
!seed_pack.json

# ── THE SIDECAR HAZARD — read before building a tarball ─────────────────────
# `*.db-wal` / `*.db-shm` above keep git clean, and that is exactly why they are
# dangerous at PACKAGING time: git cannot see them, so nothing warns you.
# MEASURED — opening the shipped schema-only DB READ-ONLY creates both:
#     sqlite3.connect("file:claude_memory_blank.db?mode=ro", uri=True)   -> creates
#     sqlite3.connect("file:claude_memory_blank.db?immutable=1", uri=True) -> does NOT
# So any inspection of the blank DB before `tar` leaves two stray files in the
# package, invisible to `git status`. Two rules follow:
#   1. Read a packaged DB with `immutable=1`, never `mode=ro`.
#   2. Sweep before tarring:  find . -name '*.db-wal' -o -name '*.db-shm' -delete
# The package gates walk the FILESYSTEM, not the index, so they DO see these —
# which is the whole reason a gate's population must come from the mechanism
# that lays the artifact rather than from `git ls-files`.

# ── THIS MACHINE, NOT THE PACKAGE ───────────────────────────────────────────
# This repository is the package, not a mirror of any one machine. Anything that
# describes THIS host, or wires it to a second brain, stays on disk and out of the
# index. The installer's hardware sweep writes a manifest for whatever machine it
# lands on; shipping one would assert someone else's GPU.
voidloom_manifest.json

# PROVISIONAL, not abandoned. Cross-brain bridges link TWO brains; voidloom ships
# with one. So the module stays out of what a recipient gets until it is proven
# worth supporting; a maintainer's local copy is ignored here so it cannot be
# committed by accident. Excision is safe by construction: claude_memory.py:429-434 already wraps the
# import and sets the module to None with "graceful: cross-tier enrichment
# silently skipped", its one consumer at :1632 is gated on `is not None`, and the
# three test classes are @unittest.skipUnless. The migrations STAY tracked, so a
# future re-enable finds its tables already built.
organs/cross_tier_bridges.py

# ── LOCAL OPERATIONAL ARTIFACTS — never in a distributable package ──────────
# _preimages/ holds database snapshots taken before a destructive landing on THIS
# machine, plus the merged_ids sidecar naming which rows that landing promoted.
# Both are facts about one apply on one brain. The .db was already excluded by
# *.db; the sidecar was not, and reached the index through a `git add -A` --
# which is the glob #7976 forbids for exactly this reason.
_preimages/

# host-bound install state written by the shipped verbs (per machine, never shared)
voidloom_canary_ledger.json
voidloom_install_receipt.json
voidloom_preimages/

# the self-check fixture root when $VOIDLOOM_SELFCHECK_FIXTURE_DIR is unset;
# a crashed run leaves its probes behind and they are scratch, never source.
organs/.vl_selfcheck_fixtures/

# hermetic pytest boxes (ext4 under $HOME, never /tmp — several assertions read st_dev)
voidloom/.pytest_boxes/
.pytest_boxes/

# THE OPERATOR'S PERSONA DECLARATION — the file that makes this brain somebody.
# The package ships the MECHANISM and never a persona (ONBOARDING_GUIDE.md's
# central promise); this file is the prescription, and it is one machine's.
# Excluded BY NAME, never by a glob: a name encodes a decision, and only the
# decision survives someone adding a file six months from now.
persona.json

# ── THE PERSONA FORGE'S RUNTIME MARKER (written by `voidloom persona decline`) ──
persona_forge.declined

# Machine-specific files (personal backups, second-brain sync, private hooks) belong
# in your clone's own .git/info/exclude, not here: that file is never published.
